// What the other one is left holding. **The first negative `Program`-subject
// memory the game ships** — `idled_with` and `bonded_in_battle` are both
// fond, so a reader will assume the subject implies fondness and it does not.
//
// The blurb is short because the memories page has no scroll and a row is
// name + subject + blurb on one line — `no_memory_row_overflows_its_popup`
// is the gate, and the spec's longer wording overflowed it by 79px.
//
// It outlasts `vented` (a 5000 half-life against 2000, at a higher cap),
// which is why a base that answers a bad mood with nothing gets worse rather
// than better.
(
    id: "turned_on_me",
    name: "Turned on me",
    blurb: "It came at me over nothing at all.",
    valence: -7.0,
    half_life: 5000,
    subject: Program,
    strike_cap: 4,
)
